# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

# Local environment
.env
.env.*
# ...but the template is not a secret and is the only record of what a
# deployment needs. AUTH_ENABLED now defaults to TRUE, so a missing variable
# fails closed rather than silently disabling authentication -- which makes
# having the list written down matter more, not less.
!.env.example
# supabase-root-2021-ca.crt is deliberately NOT ignored: it is Supabase's
# PUBLIC root CA, not a secret, and app/db.py refuses to start without it. It
# was ignored here, which is why the database connection ran with unverified
# TLS -- a deploy had no CA to verify against.
